                %li
                  %a{:href => "#equivalence_to_metric_lie_representations_2"} Equivalence to metric Lie representations
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In the construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+brane"} coincident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            (the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BLG+model"} BLG model
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ABJM+model"} ABJM model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} super
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            coupled to
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matter"} matter
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebraic
            structure appears – and at least in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BLG+model"} BLG model
            it appears at a pivotal stage in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            – which is given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multilinear+map"} trilinear map
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product+space"} inner product space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mstyle{:mathcolor => "blue"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mtext 3-bracket
                          %mrow
                            %mphantom
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  V \otimes V \otimes V
                  \\overset{
                  \\overset{
                  \\color{blue}
                  \\;\;
                  {
                  \\text{3-bracket}
                  \\atop
                  \\phantom{-}
                  }
                  
                  \\;\;
                  }{
                  [-,-,-]
                  }
                  }{\longrightarrow} V
          %p
            that is subject to some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
            which are different from but clearly reminiscent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
          %p
            In special cases, but not generally, this algebraic structure is a special case of a structure introduced by Filippov, which could be called a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Filippov+algebra"} Filippov algebra
            %em 3-Lie algebra
            or a
            %em Lie 3-algebra
            or often just a
            = succeed "." do
              %em 3-algebra
          %p
            Unfortunately, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebras"} L-infinity algebras
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorifications
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebras"} associative algebras
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-algebras"} n-algebras
            – but the structure seen in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BLG+model"} BLG model
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            is
            %em none
            of these.
          %p
            Hence to be on the safe side, one may want to speak of
            %em M2-brane 3-algebras
            or maybe
            = succeed "," do
              %em M-brane algebras
          %p
            Moreover, while this “M2-brane 3-algebra” appeared to be a central ingredient in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BLG+model"} BLG model
            %em no
            appearance in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ABJM+model"} ABJM model
          %p
            Indeed, inspection reveals that “M2-brane 3-algebras” give rise to and may be re-constructed from data in ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} Lie theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
            consisting of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+algebra"} metric Lie algebra
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+object"} dualizable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+representation"} Lie algebra representation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                  %mtext M2-brane 3-algebras
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mo ↔
                    %mo ≃
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mtext faithful orthogonal representations
                      %mrow
                        %mtext of metric Lie algebras
                    %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\big\{
                  \\text{M2-brane 3-algebras}
                  \\big\}
                  \\;\;\overset{\simeq}{\leftrightarrow}
                  \\left\{
                  {
                  \\text{faithful orthogonal representations}
                  \\atop
                  \\text{of metric Lie algebras}
                  }
                  \\right\}
          %p
            This is due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#dMFFMER08"} dMFFMER 08, Theorem 11
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#M2Brane3AlgebrasEquivalentToMetricLieRepresentation"}
            below.
          %p (…)
          %h2#definition Definition
          #AxiomsOnM2Brane3Algebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane+3-algebra"}> M2-brane 3-algebra
                )
            %p
              An
              %em M2-brane 3-algebra
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional vector space
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %em metric
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle
                  on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product+space"} inner product space
                  (not required to be positive definite);
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multilinear+map"} trilinear function
                  %em 3-bracket
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⊗
