          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#dMFFMER08"} dMFFMER 08, Prop. 10 and Theorem 11
          %h3#RelationToLieAlgebraWeightSystemsOnChordDiagrams Relation to Lie algebra weight systems on chord diagrams
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Penrose+notation"} Penrose notation
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"}> string diagram
            \-notation), the trilinear bracket induced by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+representation"} metric Lie representation
            according to Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TrilinearMapInducedFromOrthogonalRepOfMetricLieAlgebra"}
            looks as follows:
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/MBrane3AlgebraFromMetricLieRepresentationII.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %p
            With Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#M2Brane3AlgebrasEquivalentToMetricLieRepresentation"}
            this shows that M2-brane 3-algebras are equivalently the datum that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+systems"} Lie algebra weight systems
            on (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagram"}> horizontal
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagrams"} chord diagrams
            assign to a single chord.
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
          %h2#references References
          %h3#appearance_in_m2brane_theory Appearance in M2-brane theory
          %p
            The idea that some higher-arity version of the Lie bracket may be relevant for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-M5+brane+intersections"} M2-M5 brane intersections
            originates with attempts of generalizing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nahm%27s+equations"} Nahm's equations
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+funnels"} fuzzy funnels
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D2-D4+brane+intersections"} D2-D4 brane intersections
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anirban+Basu"}> Anirban Basu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Harvey"} Jeffrey Harvey
              = succeed "," do
                %em The M2-M5 Brane System and a Generalized Nahm’s Equation
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0412310"} arXiv:hep-th/0412310
          %p
            Motivated by this, the M2-brane 3-algebra appears in the construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BLG+model"} BLG model
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            on 2 coincident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            in
          %ul
            %li#BaggerLambert06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Bagger"}> Jonathan Bagger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Lambert"} Neil Lambert
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Modeling Multiple M2’s
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0611108"} hep-th/0611108
            %li#BaggerLambert07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Bagger"}> Jonathan Bagger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Lambert"} Neil Lambert
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gauge Symmetry and Supersymmetry of Multiple M2-Branes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arXiv.org/abs/0711.0955"} arXiv:0711.0955
          %p further highlighted as such in
          %ul
            %li#Gustavsson07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Gustavsson"}> Andreas Gustavsson
              ,
              %em Algebraic structures on parallel M2-branes
              Nucl. Phys. B811, 66-76 (2009) (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0709.1260"}> arXiv:0709.1260
              )
          %p
            (whence the “BLG” of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BLG+model"} BLG model
          %p and further explored in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+de+Medeiros"}> Paul de Medeiros
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"} José Figueroa-O'Farrill
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elena+M%C3%A9ndez-Escobar"} Elena Méndez-Escobar
              = succeed "," do
                %em Metric Lie 3-algebras in Bagger-Lambert theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0806.3242"} arXiv:0806.3242
          %p From here on a myriad of references followed up. Review includes:
          %p (…)
          %h3#equivalence_to_metric_lie_representations_2 Equivalence to metric Lie representations
          %p
            The full generalized axioms on the M2-brane 3-algebra and first insights into their relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+representations"} Lie algebra representations
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+algebras"} metric Lie algebras
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#CherkisSaemann08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+Cherkis"}> Sergey Cherkis
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"} Christian Saemann
              = succeed "," do
                %em Multiple M2-branes and Generalized 3-Lie algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0807.0808"} arXiv:0807.0808
          %p
            The full identification of M2-brane 3-algebras with dualizable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+representations"} Lie algebra representations
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+algebras"} metric Lie algebras
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#dMFFMER08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+de+Medeiros"}> Paul de Medeiros
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"} José Figueroa-O'Farrill
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elena+M%C3%A9ndez-Escobar"} Elena Méndez-Escobar
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patricia+Ritter"} Patricia Ritter
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the Lie-algebraic origin of metric 3-algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0809.1086"} arXiv:0809.1086
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"}> José Figueroa-O'Farrill
              , slide 145 onwards in:
              %em Triple systems and Lie superalgebras
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %em M2-branes, ADE and Lie superalgebras
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~jmf/CV/Seminars/Hongo.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/FigueroaOFarrillM2Branes02.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p further explored in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"}> José Figueroa-O'Farrill
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Simplicity in the Faulkner construction
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0905.4900"} arXiv:0905.4900
          %p
            and putting to use the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Faulkner+construction"} Faulkner construction
            that was previously introduced in
          %ul
            %li#Faulkner73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Faulkner"}> John Faulkner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the geometry of inner ideals
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693(73)90032-X"} doi:10.1016/0021-8693(73)90032-X
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Sam Palmer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"} Christian Saemann
                = succeed "," do
                  %em M-brane Models from Non-Abelian Gerbes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.5757"} arXiv:1203.5757
            %li#SaemannRitter13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patricia+Ritter"}> Patricia Ritter
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"} Christian Saemann
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie 2-algebra models
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.4892"} arXiv:1308.4892
            %li#Saemann16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"}> Christian Saemann
                , appendix A of
                %em Lectures on Higher Structures in M-Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.09815"}> arXiv:1609.09815
                )
          %p and
          %ul
            %li#Palmkvist09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jakob+Palmkvist"}> Jakob Palmkvist
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Three-algebras, triple systems and 3-graded Lie superalgebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0905.2468"} arXiv:0905.2468
